turns.replyText:
There isn’t a separate review breakdown just for first-time mattress buyers, but the overall feedback on the Matelas Hybride is very positive, with a rating of about 4.5/5.

People mainly praise:

the balance between soft comfort and firm support;
good support when sleeping in different positions;
breathability, especially for a cooler night’s sleep;
reduced movement disturbance when sharing the bed.

A useful beginner note: your body may need time to adjust. Tediber says many people notice an improvement from the first night, but full adaptation can take around 2 to 3 weeks.

That’s why the 100-night home trial is reassuring: you can judge it over real nights rather than a quick test in a shop.
